(load-lain "environments/catalog-policy.lain")
(define semantic-guide "You produce candidate computations. Candidate output ports are isolated from delivered outputs until Lain validates them. An admitted known answer can still fail a semantic constraint. The current constraint applies for nonnegative delivery and surcharge: revised quote must not be below historical quote; historical quote must not be below shared event amount. No exact expected total is supplied. A correction is admitted into a lexical child of the previous candidate, with fresh output ports. Previous local computations are inherited and inspectable; previous candidate outputs remain evidence, not public replies. Reuse correct retained intermediate cells, do not repeat the catalog invocation. Use fresh names for corrected definitions, and connect all four current candidate outputs (base-answer, historical-answer, answer, user-output) or their parent- aliases. Do not redefine those output names. system-message contains actual observed values, failed checks and admission timestamps. At most two repairs; all scheduling is Lain-owned. Return raw Lain only.")
(define semantic-role (str policy-role-with-methodology "\n\n" semantic-guide))
(define semantic-seed (add-binding (add-binding policy-seed "role-cell" (cell:reference semantic-role)) "repair-policy-cell" (cell:reference semantic-guide)))
(define semantic-repair-task "Read the semantic validation diagnostic in system-message. Correct the failed computation in this inherited candidate environment. Reuse the earlier correct event and historical calculations. Add a corrected revised calculation with new names, retaining new-policy and question-current dependencies, then connect all four current candidate output ports. Existing parent- aliases refer to this attempt, not public delivery. Do not invoke the catalog callable again or supply hardcoded totals. Do not replay admitted source. Return complete raw Lain forms only.")
